            <ArticleTitle>Raphe nucleus encephalopathy (myalgic encephalomyelitis, epidemic neuromyasthenia).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>351-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An injury to the dorsal raphe nucleus by Coxsackie B viruses is suggested as the cause of the disease sometimes called myalgic encephalomyelitis. The signs and symptoms are consistent with a serotonin deficiency in the dorsal raphe nucleus and the disease has a predisposition for women in nursing. Stress and underlying tryptophan deficiencies are considered as contributory factors.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
